OS Concepts with Linux
----------------------

what is os ?
	
	OS is a software that controls hardware.

	Advantages
	----------
	
	* Multitasking
	
	* Manage the resources effectively

	* Resource allocate / resource manager

why linux ?

	It will support for around 20 architecture and linux is open source.

What are the components of OS ?

	1. Application 
	
	2. Services	

	Kernel is called the core of an operating system. 
	Services are mandatory. 
	Applications are optional

	
Booting process of Linux

	1.BIOS (Basic Input Output System) 
		
		present in ROM chip, manufacture burns one program into ROM  chip called BIOS.

		BIOS will check that before loading OS, it will check if basic input/output system like hdd, RAM etc ... is present or not, then only to proceed ahead otherwise not.

	2.If everthing is ok Then Bios will run one program called MBR (Master Boot Record) (a file of 12 bytes) present in the starting portion of HDD. 

	3.MBR executes GRUB (Grand Unified bootloader).

	4.GRUB will load kernel.

	5.Kernel will load all the services. (load some temp file system, mount the file system).

	6.Its starts the service called init.

	7.Run level program
		
		init process initiates all services. 
		All the services (drivers) are loaded in to the RAM.

	Init is the first process created and then it initiates the another services. 



Process and Process Management
------------------------------

* The program which is in execution is called process.	

* The executable file which is loaded into the RAM for execution technically, we call as process. 

* Life of an executeable file ends when we intentionally remove it by "rm" command or overwrite it. 

* CPU execute the instruction as all the code present in the RAM.

* If multiple processing environment, multiple process executes process executes simultaneously.


